# Test: ze doctor --json reports a managed client listener that cannot bind
#
# VALIDATES: spec-managed-server-hardening AC-3 -- a hub server block that
#            declares managed clients on the address the plugin acceptor binds
#            is reported through the operator's own entry point.
# PREVENTS: a hub that reads as configured and serves no managed client, because
#           the acceptor took the address first and the managed listener was
#           skipped with only a log line.
#
# doctor-hub-managed-separate.ci is the control: the same check MUST stay silent
# on the central-hub configuration that works. One file for each, because every
# expect= line in a .ci is evaluated against the LAST command's output.

tmpfs=hub-collision.conf:terminator=EOF_COLLISION
plugin {
    hub {
        server local {
            ip 127.0.0.1;
            port 12790;
            secret abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz012345;
            client edge-01 { secret 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef; }
        }
    }
}
EOF_COLLISION

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json hub-collision.conf
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-hub-managed-collision
expect=stdout:contains=127.0.0.1:12790
